EXPERIMENTAL: capture Scene as LDR instead of HDR.

PIPCamera.cpp sets CaptureSource = SCS_FinalToneCurveHDR for Scene and Lighting while every
other image type uses SCS_FinalColorLDR. FinalToneCurveHDR returns values after the tone curve
but before the final LDR/sRGB encode, and AirSim then packs that into an 8-bit buffer.

Observed (drone-sim, 2026-08-03): AirSim's Scene capture of the City Park world looks washed
out and low-contrast, while Unreal's own HighResShot of the same world looks correct. Six
world-side interventions -- DefaultScalability.ini, SM5 to SM6, a UE4 to UE5 package
conversion, and replacing the deprecated AtmosphericFog -- changed the AirSim output not at
all, which points downstream of the world entirely.

THIS PATCH IS NOT YET VALIDATED. It is the obvious candidate given the asymmetry above, but
attempts to characterise the fault quantitatively were repeatedly confounded (different
viewpoints, the vehicle falling between captures, FPV viewport not matching front_center,
letterboxing), so it is being tested empirically rather than argued for.

It is also a DECISION, not purely a bug fix. HDR capture is arguably right for perception work
that wants dynamic range. What is not defensible is packing an HDR buffer into 8 bits, which
discards the range AND mis-encodes it. If HDR is wanted, the right form is float output
(pixels_as_float), not uint8.

NOTE ON LINE ENDINGS: Cosys-AirSim sources are CRLF. This hunk was generated from the real
file, not hand-written.

